From: Artem Butusov <art.sormy@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] dtc: add -P to print phandle references as &label

When converting a blob back to source, dtc prints phandle cells as raw
numbers because the DTB records no reference information. The data needed
to recover it is still there: __symbols__ carries the label names, and
#<specifier>-cells on each target gives the group width.

Add -P/--phandle-refs, which walks the well-known phandle-bearing
properties and adds the REF_PHANDLE markers the writer already knows how
to print, so "clocks = <0x02 0xaf>" comes back as "clocks = <&cru 0xaf>".

A property is only marked when the walk consumes its value exactly; any
mismatch leaves it untouched and numeric. Explicit phandle properties are
preserved, so the output recompiles to a byte-identical blob.

Signed-off-by: Artem Butusov <art.sormy@gmail.com>
---
